From 9dfa93db8417545d61747394cd99f63e0e4d8e50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: romainhedouin <romain.hedouin@epitech.eu>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:07:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/mpegts: read the PID at the sync byte in analyze()

The PID was read from buf + 1, i.e. always from the first packet,
while the adaptation field control on the next line is read at the
current sync byte (buf + i). The null-packet check in probe mode thus
used the wrong packet.

Tested: make fate passes. Probing all 2569 files of the FATE suite
gives the same detected format and score before and after.

Signed-off-by: romainhedouin <romain.hedouin@epitech.eu>

(cherry picked from commit 9dfa93db8417545d61747394cd99f63e0e4d8e50)
Upstream: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/9dfa93db8417545d61747394cd99f63e0e4d8e50
---
 libavformat/mpegts.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/mpegts.c b/libavformat/mpegts.c
index 713e19d..b3b13dc 100644
--- a/libavformat/mpegts.c
+++ b/libavformat/mpegts.c
@@ -654,7 +654,7 @@ static int analyze(const uint8_t *buf, int size, int packet_size,
 
     for (i = 0; i < size - 3; i++) {
         if (buf[i] == SYNC_BYTE) {
-            int pid = AV_RB16(buf+1) & 0x1FFF;
+            int pid = AV_RB16(buf + i + 1) & 0x1FFF;
             int asc = buf[i + 3] & 0x30;
             if (!probe || pid == 0x1FFF || asc) {
                 int x = i % packet_size;
